# Redirects for Cloudflare Pages.
#
# THIS FILE IS DELIBERATELY EMPTY OF RULES. Read on before adding one.
#
# What it used to contain, and why it is gone:
#
#   https://www.kaskalba.com/*  https://kaskalba.com/:splat  301
#
# That rule never fired. Measured on the live domain 2026-11-26, once
# www.kaskalba.com had been added as a second custom domain: every path on
# www answered 200 with the page itself, not a 301 to the apex. Cloudflare
# Pages matches the source as a PATH; a source carrying a hostname matches
# nothing, and it fails silently rather than erroring at build time.
#
# A hostname-level redirect therefore cannot live here. It lives in the
# dashboard as a Redirect Rule — see _src/MIGRATION-CLOUDFLARE.md §4ج for
# the exact settings.
#
# The other obvious rule, /privacy.html to /privacy and its two siblings,
# is not here either and must not be added: Cloudflare Pages already does
# it, verified returning 308. A hand-written duplicate of a built-in is a
# rule nobody remembers is there.
#
# So the file stays, empty, as the place that explains where the redirects
# actually are. Deleting it would only invite someone to recreate the rule
# that does not work.
